  "generated_text": "To solve the equation $\\frac{r+9}{r-3} = \\frac{r-2}{r+5}$, we can start by cross-multiplying to eliminate the fractions. This gives us:\n\n$(r+9)(r+5) = (r-2)(r-3)$\n\nExpanding both sides, we get:\n\n$r^2 + 14r + 45 = r^2 - 5r + 6$\n\nSubtracting $r^2$ from both sides and adding $5r$ to both sides, we get:\n\n$19r + 39 = 6$\n\nSubtracting $39$ from both sides, we get:\n\n$19r = -33$\n\nDividing both sides by $19$, we get:\n\n$r = \\frac{-33}{19}$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the equation is $r = \\boxed{\\frac{-33}{19}}$.",
  "grade": {
